+# BLUE CURRENT V51.55.0 — PILOT LAUNCH CONTROL
+
+V51.51–V51.55 adds the final human-controlled launch gate between a certified pilot deployment package and an actual restaurant pilot.
+
+## Launch-control gates
+
+Each pilot location is evaluated against 10 launch gates:
+
+1. PILOT_LOCATION_SELECTED
+2. DEPLOYMENT_PACKAGE_CERTIFIED
+3. CONFIGURATION_FROZEN
+4. CONFIGURATION_UNCHANGED
+5. LAUNCH_WINDOW
+6. LAUNCH_OWNER
+7. OPERATOR_ROSTER
+8. SUPPORT_BRIDGE
+9. NO_OPEN_BLOCKERS
+10. PRELAUNCH_EVIDENCE
+
+## Configuration freeze
+
+When launch control is configured, Blue Current snapshots the pilot restaurant configuration and stores a SHA-256 fingerprint across:
+
+- location identity/status
+- tables
+- sections
+- scoped memberships
+- connector configuration/status
+
+Before authorization, the current configuration is compared against the frozen hash.
+
+If configuration changes after the freeze, the launch gate reopens.
+
+## Pilot launch ownership
+
+Launch control requires:
+
+- launch owner
+- launch window start
+- launch window end
+- confirmed pilot operator roster
+- live support bridge/channel
+- support owner
+- escalation owner
+- human pre-launch evidence
+
+## Launch blockers
+
+Human launch blockers can be recorded during configuration.
+
+Any unresolved blocker prevents launch authorization.
+
+Resolving a blocker requires human resolution evidence.
+
+## Human authorization
+
+Final state:
+
+`PILOT_LAUNCH_AUTHORIZED`
+
+Authorization requires:
+
+- all 10 launch gates passing
+- admin permission
+- human authorization evidence
+- human authorization note
+
+Authorization is deliberately separate from execution.
+
+It does not:
+
+- start the runtime
+- execute a deployment
+- perform go-live
+- modify restaurant operating state
+
+## Current authenticated Chefs runtime
+
+Current untouched authoritative state:
+
+`pilot-launch-control-required`
+
+All five locations currently show 1/10 launch gates passing because no V51 launch-control record or deployment-package certification has yet been written to the authoritative database.
+
+The one passing gate is:
+
+- zero unresolved launch blockers
+
+Marina Grille remains the logical first pilot candidate because it is the most complete restaurant configuration from the prior V51 deployment/readiness waves, but V51.55 does not choose or authorize it automatically.
+
+## Safety policy
+
+- one pilot location at a time recommended
+- configuration freeze required
+- deployment package certification required
+- operator roster confirmation required
+- support bridge required
+- zero open blockers required
+- human launch authorization required
+- authorization does not start runtime
+- authorization does not perform go-live
+- automatic launch false
+- automatic go-live false
+- autonomous production changes false
+
+## Validation
+
+- V51.55 focused launch-control lifecycle PASS
+- pilot-location selection PASS
+- configuration freeze PASS
+- configuration drift detection PASS
+- pre-launch verification PASS
+- launch window PASS
